-- Negative golden: a builtin with no JS-target mapping must be a COMPILE
-- error (pinned diagnostic on stderr), not a silent bare-call emit that
-- throws ReferenceError at runtime. int_max_value is doubly unsupported:
-- its value (2^62 - 1) is not representable in the JS target's double-backed
-- Int, so it gets the tailored message.
mod JsUnmappedBuiltin do
  fn main() : Unit do
    println(int_to_string(int_max_value(())))
  end
end
